// THIS FILE'S IDENTITY (grep: "keyed as" | "derives from" | "grounded in")

this is a template for "OmniCode Code (4-Block Executable)":
    keyed as "B-word-omni-seed-code"
    following "4-Block Structure"

this template classifies as:
    independent (1) when "using standard library only"
    connected (0) when "needing internal modules" such as "[list them]"
    dependent (-1) when "requiring external packages" such as "[list them]"

this template derives from:
    original (1) when "establishing new 4-block pattern beyond universal"
    derived (0) from "B-word-omni-seed-universal" because "implements universal template for code files"
    variant (-1) when "intentionally departing from universal standard"
    documented at "bereshit/word/omni/seed/universal.omni"

this template strictness is:
    tight (1) meaning "Follow exactly - 4-block structure, required sections"
    guided (0) meaning "Adapt thoughtfully - implementation within structure"
    free (-1) meaning "Principles only - teaching comments, examples"

to use this template:
    copy and modify for new OmniCode files
    replace [bracketed] placeholders with actual content
    change pragma from "template" to "code" when ready to compile
    remove this preamble section when ready

    meaning "4-block code template - the structure all executable/library files follow"
    teaching "METADATA → SETUP → BODY → CLOSING; each block has tiers and sections"

grounded in:
    scripture "In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth"
        from Genesis 1:1 in KJV
    principle "Structure enables creation - boundaries before content"
    anchor "And God saw every thing that he had made, and, behold, it was very good"
        from Genesis 1:31 in KJV

serves as:
    Rails (foundation) for "All OmniCode code files derive structure from this template"
    role "Code template defining 4-block pattern for executable/library files"

authored by:
    architect "Seanje Lenox-Wise"
    implementation "Nova Dawn"
    created "2025-11-01"
    version "1.0.0"
    modified "2025-12-17" with "Header addition, chain fix, native constructs"

exists to:
    purpose "Define 4-block structure for all code files"
    features:
        "4-block pattern (METADATA → SETUP → BODY → CLOSING)"
        "Tiered organization within blocks"
        "Schema patterns with meaning/teaching constructs"
    design "Template by example - structure IS the specification"
    philosophy "Code as covenant - executable files that honor commitments"

interface of this template:
    depends on:
        requires (1): "bereshit/word/omni/seed/universal.omni" for "universal patterns"
        includes (0): "Genesis 1 creation pattern" for "structural foundation"
        excludes (-1): "Format-specific syntax - this is format-agnostic"
    integrated as:
        import "Format templates (library.go, library.c) derive from this"
        pattern "Copy template, fill schemas, change pragma to code"

operational context:
    blocking:
        yes (1) because "Changes here affect all downstream code templates"
    health:
        system Base100 with scale from -100 to +100
        granted (1) above +50 meaning "Template is complete and aligned with universal"
        deferred (0) within ±50 meaning "Template in refinement"
        denied (-1) below -50 meaning "Template has structural inconsistencies"

