core identity of this work:

    grounded in:
        meaning "Biblical foundation - every code file is grounded in Scripture"
        teaching "Scripture establishes purpose, principle embodies it, anchor reinforces"

        scripture: <verse establishing WHY this code exists - theological foundation>
            from: <Book Chapter:Verse> in <KJV or WEB>
        principle: <1-sentence Kingdom principle this code embodies>
        anchor: <supporting verse that reinforces the principle>
            from: <Book Chapter:Verse> in <KJV or WEB>

    serves as <Ladder|Baton|Rails>:
        meaning "Architectural role - where this code sits in the system"
        teaching "Ladder = entry point | Baton = passed dependency | Rails = foundation"

        role: <specific architectural responsibility - what this code DOES in the system>
        paradigm "CPI-SI framework"

    authored by:
        meaning "Attribution and versioning - who created what, when"

        architect: <person who designed the approach/requirements>
        implementation: <person who wrote and verified the code>
        created: <YYYY-MM-DD when file was first created>
        version: <semantic version - MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH>
        modified: <YYYY-MM-DD> with <brief description of what changed>

    exists to:
        meaning "Purpose and capabilities - why this code exists and what it enables"

        purpose: <1-sentence answer to "what problem does this code solve?">
        design: <architectural pattern or paradigm this code follows>
        philosophy: <guiding principle - the WHY behind design decisions>
        features:
            <capability 1 - what this code provides>
            <capability 2 - what this code enables>
            <capability 3 - what problems this code solves>

interface of this work:

    depends on:
        meaning "Dependencies and relationships - what this code needs and what needs it"
        teaching "Ternary: requires (must have) | includes (nice to have) | excludes (conflicts)"

        requires (1): <hard dependency - code breaks without this> for <why it's needed>
        includes (0): <soft dependency - enhances but not required> for <what it adds>
        excludes (-1): <conflict - cannot coexist with> because <why incompatible>
        used by: <what commands/libraries/tools consume this code>
        integrates with: <cross-component interactions>

    integrated as:
        meaning "How this code is invoked - the execution pattern"
        teaching "Command syntax, arguments, and exit codes for covenant fulfillment"

        command: <executable-name> <args> for <what it does>
        command: <executable-name> --help for "show usage"
        exits 0 (1) for "success - covenant fulfilled"
        exits 1 (0) for "partial - completed with warnings"
        exits 2 (-1) for "failure - covenant broken"

operational context of this work:

    blocking:
        meaning "Does this code block operations while it runs?"
        teaching "yes (1) = operations wait | conditional (0) = depends | no (-1) = non-blocking"

        <yes (1)|conditional (0)|no (-1)> because <why this code does/doesn't block>
        mitigation: <how blocking/failures are handled>

    health:
        meaning "Base100 health scoring - universal metric for code wellness"
        teaching "All code files scored -100 to +100; operations and weights vary by purpose"

        system Base100 with scale from -100 to +100
        granted (1) above +50 meaning "covenant established"
        deferred (0) within ±50 meaning "in process"
        denied (-1) below -50 meaning "covenant broken"

        operations:
            <operation that adds health> scores +<points> (1) for <why it's positive>
            <operation that's neutral> scores 0 (0) for <why no change>
            <operation that reduces health> scores -<points> (-1) for <why it's negative>

        cascade multipliers:
            <category of impact> multiplies by <factor> because <why this amplifies/dampens>

